   "name": "Freight Rework & Transloading Operations",
   "description": "Freight rework and transloading operations from The Flat Rate Movers: the corrective freight-handling service for loads that cannot move as they sit, plus planned mode-change and dock-to-dock freight work on the I-81 corridor, dispatched from Winchester, VA and Martinsburg, WV. Company scope (published): freight reworks — loads refused or rejected at a receiver's dock are rebuilt so they can deliver; load-shift correction — freight that shifted in transit is stabilized, unloaded under control, restacked and re-secured; damaged-freight separation — crushed, torn or water-damaged cases are pulled and documented while the good freight is rebuilt to deliver; overweight and axle correction — freight is repositioned, redistributed between axles, partially offloaded and reloaded, or split so the truck can legally roll; collapsed and failed pallets are repalletized onto sound pallets; floor-loaded freight is palletized to the receiver's specification. Callers are freight professionals — drivers and owner-operators, carriers and their dispatchers and operations managers, freight brokers, 3PLs, warehouses and receivers. The work is performed where the job requires: the company's leased space, the receiver's dock, or a yard. Emergency and after-hours response is available at premium rates; every job is scoped and quoted at one flat rate before work begins, and no rate, range or fee schedule is published for this service. Planned work under the same category: cross-docking — inbound freight transferred directly to outbound vehicles, sorted and consolidated dock to dock, typically turned in under 24 hours with little to no storage; transloading — freight transferred between transportation modes, ocean container or railcar to domestic truck, with floor-loaded contents repalletized, sorted or held in short staging before the switch; rail-to-truck transfer work at rail-served locations when contracted. Heavy equipment manipulation — repositioning machinery and heavy crated freight inside trailers, containers and dock space — runs under the same handling discipline as the company's SIR Structural Integrity Relocation work for high-mass assets of 1,500 to 3,500 lbs, in the freight setting. Equipment varies by project; trucks are leased. The category absorbs the company's published transloading services as its children — container deconsolidation, cross-docking and transloading, Winchester transloading, and Virginia Inland Port transloading — without duplicating them. Guaranteed Flat Rate or Your Move is Free!",
